
= Outreach
I take part in outreach events, directed mostly towards girls, to encourage them to overcome stereotypes and engage in long scientific studies, because science is awesome!

=== Event organisation 
*2020, 2019: Young Women Mathematician and Computer Scientists Days (Inria Paris)*
\nDuring these two days, high school girls discover how to do research in mathematics by working on challenging open problem under supervision, attend talks by women scientists and meet women Ph.D. and post-docs, to discover possible futures in maths and computer science. 
\n[https://www.di.ens.fr/eloise.berthier/index.html Eloise Berthier] and I co-organised and hosted the Inria Paris 2020 event; [https://who.paris.inria.fr/Matthieu.Lequesne/index.php Matthieu Lequesne] helped us for the 2019 edition. 

=== Speed meetings
*2020: Girls and math: a luminous equation (Sorbonne, Online)*
\nTook part in several speed meetings between girls and researchers to talk about math and computer science careers ([https://filles-et-maths.fr/journees-filles-et-maths/ Event description])

*2020: Engineers in the classroom (Lycée Jean Moulin)*
\nDescribed to high school students what the job of a software engineer is, as well as different interesting machine learning uses and ethical questions in daily life.

=== Programming introduction
*2019: Highschool students summer school (ESPCI)*
\nIntroduced the different jobs of computer science engineer to high school girls, and animated an introductory software development workshop in Python over an afternoon. ([https://www.espci.fr/fr/actualites/2019/lyceennes-une-ecole-d-ete-juste-pour-vous Event description])

